! legacy_particles3d.nml — Mera test fixture: the LEGACY (pversion = 0) particle format
!
! *** THIS ONE MUST BE RUN WITH AN OLD RAMSES, NOT 2026.05 ***
!
! Build it from the `stable_17_09` BRANCH of github.com/ramses-organisation/ramses:
!     RAMSES_SRC=<clone of stable_17_09> BUILD_DIR=/tmp/rbuild_17_09 NDIMS=3 MPI=1 \
!         bash build_ramses.sh
! It still compiles with gfortran 15 given the -fallow-argument-mismatch / -fallow-invalid-boz
! flags that build_ramses.sh applies (verified 2026-08).
!
! WHY. Mera's particle reader branches on the header signature (src/read_data/RAMSES/getinfo.jl):
!     "Total"  in header_*.txt  ->  version 0   the LEGACY layout
!     "Family" in header_*.txt  ->  version 1   the modern layout
! MEASURED BOUNDARY — the code comment in getinfo.jl says "=< stable_18_09" for Total, which is
! off by one release: stable_17_09 writes "Total number of particles" (version 0), while
! stable_18_09 ALREADY writes the Family header (version 1). This fixture therefore needs 17_09.
! Every fixture generated with 2026.05 exercises version 1 only. This one is the regression guard
! for version 0 — the path currently covered only by a 14 GB private simulation. A modern RAMSES
! cannot emit it; an old one can, and the old one still builds.
!
! THE ORACLE IS THE INPUT FILE. Particles come from a hand-written ascii file (make_legacy_
! particles.sh): a 4x4x4 lattice, zero velocity, DISTINCT masses m_i = 1e-3 * i, total 2.08
! exactly. With no gravity and no motion, Mera must read back exactly 64 particles at exactly
! those positions with exactly those masses, in every snapshot. Nothing is copied from a previous
! run, so this is a real oracle and not a golden master.
!
! NOTE ON COORDINATES: load_ascii adds boxlen/2 to each position, so the file holds coordinates
! relative to the BOX CENTRE while Mera reports them in [0, boxlen].
!
! Prepare and run:
!     bash make_legacy_particles.sh > ic_part      # the name MUST be ic_part
!     mpirun -np 4 /tmp/rbuild_17_09/bin/ramses3d legacy_particles3d.nml > run.log 2>&1
!
! MEASURED (RAMSES stable_17_09, 4 ranks): 3 outputs, 6.6 MB, < 1 s.
!   header_*.txt begins "Total number of particles / 64"      -> Mera reports pversion = 0
!   getparticles returns 64 rows with the LEGACY column set
!       (:x,:y,:z,:id,:vx,:vy,:vz,:mass,:birth)
!   versus the MODERN set from a 2026.05 fixture
!       (:level,:x,:y,:z,:id,:family,:tag,:vx,:vy,:vz,:mass,:birth)
!   total mass 2.080000000000000, identical to the ascii input; per-particle max|diff| = 6.9e-18
!   positions recover the 4x4x4 lattice at x in {0.125,0.375,0.625,0.875} (shifted by boxlen/2)

&RUN_PARAMS
hydro=.true.
pic=.true.
poisson=.false.
static=.true.
nrestart=0
nremap=0
ncontrol=1
nsubcycle=10*1
verbose=.false.
/

&AMR_PARAMS
levelmin=5
levelmax=5
ngridmax=50000
npartmax=10000
nexpand=1
boxlen=1.0
/

&INIT_PARAMS
filetype='ascii'
initfile(1)='.'
nregion=1
region_type(1)='square'
x_center=0.5
y_center=0.5
z_center=0.5
length_x=10.0
length_y=10.0
length_z=10.0
exp_region=10.0
d_region=1.0
u_region=0.0
v_region=0.0
w_region=0.0
p_region=1.0
/

&OUTPUT_PARAMS
noutput=2
tout=0.01,0.02
/

&HYDRO_PARAMS
gamma=1.6666667
courant_factor=0.8
scheme='muscl'
slope_type=1
/

&REFINE_PARAMS
/
